{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And by these you become impure.</b> [Refers to] 'every creeping thing of the bird [with] four legs' and 'these you shall detest among the birds.' Others say that 'these' refers to 'every beast' and 'everything that walks on paws.' In my opinion, the word 'these' refers to all those mentioned above." "<b>You become impure.</b> From the binyan of hithpa'el; the dagesh in the tet is because the tav is absorbed. Likewise 'and he heard the voice speaking to him' and 'the one who purifies shall wash his garments.'" "<b>He is impure until evening.</b> Scripture held to a terse course, for he must wash in water."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The two examples illustrate the same phonological phenomenon (assimilation of tav) in different forms: וישמע את הקול מדבר (Numbers 7:89) and כבס המטהר (Leviticus 14:9, with tav-assimilated form)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:35.840550835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}